From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:55:34 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Implement wlr-gamma-control-unstable-v1

Add the zwlr_gamma_control_manager_v1 global. get_gamma_control()
sends gamma_size with the output's CRTC gamma LUT size, or failed if
the output has no gamma LUT (or no longer exists). set_gamma() reads
the three 16-bit ramps from the fd without blocking and hands them to
the output's color device as a gamma override; a table of the wrong
size is an invalid_gamma protocol error, an unreadable fd sends failed.

There is at most one active control per output. A newer control takes
over: the previous one gets failed and the output gets its own ramp
back until the new client sets one. Destroying the control, the output
going away, or the output's gamma size changing restores the ramp the
output had before (or what night light and the profile call for now).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
